 "content": [
  {
   "children": [
    "working-paper, architecture, framework"
   ],
   "tag": "aside"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A working paper written on 2026-11-16, published nearly as written. Local file paths, private repository names and personal names have been removed."
   ],
   "tag": "blockquote"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Status:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " code, 2026-10-17. Linear ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NA-24"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ", ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NA-27"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ", ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NA-270"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ". Synthetic tests only in git."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Attaches every overlapping zone or designation to each HeavyMap parcel ID with area shares. The ID registry (",
    {
     "children": [
      "industrial_atlas/ids/"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", heavymap-id-registry.md) mints the parcel keys. This package does not mint IDs and does not publish."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "the owner’s decisions that this code follows:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Store every intersecting zone (provisional). The dossier explains overlaps; this table does not simplify to a dominant class."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Join Greenbelt designation, Niagara Escarpment Plan designation, and NEP Development Control Area to every parcel, with area shares (firm)."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Labels are source-quoted (",
      {
       "children": [
        "City zoning: M11"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", ",
      {
       "children": [
        "City class: Vacant Lands"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "). HeavyMap does not assert vacancy."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Nothing here is published. Pulled rows stay in local data (not published)."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Output"
   },
   "children": [
    "Output"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Long-format CSV, one row per parcel × overlay feature intersection:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "ia_id"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: Registry parcel ID (",
      {
       "children": [
        "ia:ca:on:hamilton:parcel:{ULID}"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ")"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "layer_id"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: Overlay config id (",
      {
       "children": [
        "LYR-HAM-ZONING"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", …)"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "feature_source_id"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: Source feature id (GlobalID, OGF_ID, OBJECTID, …)"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "class"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: Source class field, or a constant such as ",
      {
       "children": [
        "urban"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " / ",
      {
       "children": [
        "regulated"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "quoted_label"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: Source-quoted label from the layer template"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "area_m2"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: Intersection area in the working CRS (EPSG:26917)"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "parcel_share"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "area_m2 / parcel_area"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "feature_share"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "area_m2 / overlay_feature_area"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      }
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "sliver"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Meaning: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "y"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " when share ",
      {
       "children": [
        "and"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " area are under the sliver caps; still kept"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Default sliver rule: ",
    {
     "children": [
      "parcel_share < 0.01"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " ",
    {
     "children": [
      "and"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " ",
    {
     "children": [
      "area_m2 < 5"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". Flagged, not dropped."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Working CRS is EPSG:26917, same as the registry. Lon/lat GeoJSON is refused."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "How-it-scales"
   },
   "children": [
    "How it scales"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Overlay polygons for ",
      {
       "children": [
        "one layer"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " sit in a shapely 2 ",
      {
       "children": [
        "STRtree"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". The tree is built once per layer, not once per chunk."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Polygons with more than 256 vertices are cut into quadrant pieces once per layer, like PostGIS ",
      {
       "children": [
        "ST_Subdivide"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". The pieces partition the feature, so their summed intersections equal the whole-feature intersection. Pieces are prepared, so a parcel that sits inside a piece takes its own area without a GEOS overlay. The remaining pairs are intersected in one vectorised call per chunk."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Registry parcels stream from ",
      {
       "children": [
        "parcels.csv"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " in chunks (default 2,500). Peak RAM is one overlay layer plus one chunk, aimed well under 2 GB on a machine with about 3–4 GB free."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Invalid geometries are repaired with ",
      {
       "children": [
        "make_valid"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " (zoning: 72 invalid, 31 missing — Q-015). Counts go in the run manifest."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Secondary-plan lot-cut polygons are ",
      {
       "children": [
        "not"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " dissolved. Each lot polygon that overlaps a parcel is a row."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Requires ",
    {
     "children": [
      "shapely 2"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ". The ID registry remains stdlib-only."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Persistence"
   },
   "children": [
    "Persistence"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Configurable directory, default local data (not published) (gitignored):"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "CURRENT\nruns/<run_id>/\n  MANIFEST.json\n  overlay_links.csv"
   ],
   "tag": "pre"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "CLI"
   },
   "children": [
    "CLI"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "python3 -m industrial_atlas.overlays \\\n  --registry-dir local data (not published) \\\n  --data-root local-data \\\n  --overlay LYR-HAM-ZONING=local data (not published)"
   ],
   "tag": "pre"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Equivalent: ",
    {
     "children": [
      "python3 scripts/link_hamilton_overlays.py"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". Missing layer paths are skipped unless ",
    {
     "children": [
      "--require-all"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". Inputs must already be in EPSG:26917."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "This cloud VM cannot reach ArcGIS. Run the linker on the owner’s machine against local pulls. Never commit those files."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
